    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A humming AC unit, that's a bit of a red flag, isn't it? It's probably a sign that something's amiss, like a mischievous little goblin trying to get your attention. You see, in the world of AC units, a humming sound without spinning is often a sign of a refrigerant leak or a faulty compressor. It's a bit like a lone goblin trying to communicate with you, but instead of a message, it's a warning that something's gone awry.\n\nAs for safety, I'd advise against going near the unit until you've had a professional take a look. You don't want to get zapped by an electrical shock or, worse, get caught in a refrigerant leak. It's like trying to navigate a dark cave without a map, you never know what kind of goblin surprises you might encounter.\n\nHowever, if you're feeling brave, you can try to locate the source of the humming sound. It's usually coming from the compressor or the condenser coils. Just be careful not to get too close, or you might end up with a face full of dust and debris, like a goblin's treasure trove.",
